{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792795223,"nonce":"CZ6lc+U5N/Kwq3/oIWSTUsKQab0=","title":"Control OBS streaming profiles, scenes and broadcast state from Jam","message":"Master roadmap: 455de32231e2b4a39765b4dff0223570b525ccec145049431e6483f5aa521f98\n\nMilestone: P2\n\nScope\nAdd the first broadcast driver using authenticated OBS WebSocket. Discover/select an existing profile and scene, preview state, start/stop and report reconnect/stream reality. Initial stream destinations/credentials may be configured in OBS; do not silently rewrite unrelated profiles, expose keys or assume a timeout means a stream stopped. Support local-only operation without a paid Jam tier and driver availability on each shipped OS.\n\nAcceptance criteria\nTests cover OBS absent, wrong password, multiple profiles, rapid repeated start/stop, OBS restart and response loss while broadcasting. UI and actual stream state reconcile safely. Calls never block editing, logs do not reveal credentials, and teardown releases only RayDE-owned connection work rather than terminating unrelated OBS sessions.\n\nAssociations and blocking dependencies are recorded below using full git-bug IDs. This issue remains open until implementation and validation are complete.","files":null}]}